     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div><br>This is not really a ggplot2 issue per se because it applies more generally to any R graphic. Here is a pointer to a recent discussion on R-help from last week:<br>\n<br></div><a href=\"http://r.789695.n4.nabble.com/Creating-publication-quality-plots-for-use-in-Microsoft-Word-td2540676.html#a2541107\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://r.789695.n4.nabble.com/Creating-publication-quality-plots-for-use-in-Microsoft-Word-td2540676.html%23a2541107&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792381866738000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0e9zrlcQNx3hGsSI2lDMBa\">http://r.789695.n4.nabble.com/Creating-publication-quality-plots-for-use-in-Microsoft-Word-td2540676.html#a2541107</a><br>\n<br>I searched R-help on Nabble with the search words &#39;pdf Word&#39; and scared up a number of hits. Hopefully this gives you some fruitful ideas.<br><br>Dennis<br><br><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"></blockquote></div>"
